# [REGEXT](../wg/regext.html)

## Summary

The REGEXT Working Group met at IETF 121. The session included status updates on published and advancing documents, a proposal for a new Working Group Last Call (WGLC) processing strategy, and presentations on active working group drafts as well as several individual proposals. Key topics included balance mappings, EPP grace period mapping updates, RDAP extensions, structured reliability scoring, EPP registry locking mechanisms, holder-designated subordinate RDAP referrals, a new suite of EPP/RDAP extension drafts, and standardized DNSSEC parameter allow-lists in EPP.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Administration, Document Status, and WGLC Process
*Presentation: [Chair Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-regext-chair-slides-00) by James Galvin*

- **Document Status**: `draft-ietf-regext-rdap-dns-ttl` has been published as an RFC, and multiple active drafts are progressing through the publication pipeline.
- **WGLC Batch Strategy**: James Galvin proposed processing mature working group drafts for WGLC in blocks of three once `draft-ietf-regext-rdap-extensions` clears. Each document will receive a separate WGLC email to prevent technical issues in one document from blocking others.
- **Prioritization Discussion**: In the chat and mic queue, Mario Loffredo, Jim Reid, Suzanne Woolf, and James Galvin discussed whether adoption and WGLC queues should follow strict first-come, first-served (FCFS) or be prioritized based on working group urgency. The chairs agreed to make the current queue visible on the mailing list for community feedback.

