### `draft-ranjbar-regext-rdap-subordinate-referrals-03`: Referrals to Holder-Designated RDAP Services
*Presentation: [Referrals to Holder-Designated RDAP Services for Subordinate Resources (draft-ranjbar-regext-rdap-subordinate-referrals-03)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-regext-referrals-to-holder-designated-rdap-services-for-subordinate-resources-draft-ranjbar-regext-rdap-subordinate-referrals-03-00) by Kaveh Ranjbar*

- **Overview**: Enables IP/ASN resource holders to designate their own subordinate RDAP services when a registry's coverage stops at the allocation boundary.
- **Updates**: Version 03 incorporates the base RDAP relationship types transferred from `draft-ietf-regext-rdap-extensions`.
- **Discussion**: Jasdip Singh supported moving the base star relationships into this draft. Jim Gould asked about applicability to domain registries. Werner Staub and Farzaneh Badii supported the work, emphasizing its utility for resource holders seeking to provide verified identity or operational metadata while preserving privacy.

