### Suite of EPP and RDAP Extensions
*Presentation: [New set of EPP and RDAP extensions](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-regext-new-set-of-epp-and-rdap-extensions-00) by James Gould*

- **Overview**: James Gould introduced five new individual specifications covering two functional areas:
  1. *Authentication Token & Status Set Extensions*: Provides JWS-signed auth tokens transferred via EPP to authorize operations on locked objects, alongside abstract status sets mapping to underlying EPP statuses.
  2. *Server Validation Extension*: Allows servers to communicate asynchronous or synchronous validation state (e.g., DNSSEC validation failures) to registrars and end users via EPP and RDAP.
- **Discussion**: Paweł Kowalski and Martin Hoffmann questioned how status sets interact with existing client status management and suggested decoupling auth token mechanisms from status sets.

