### `draft-jabley-regext-allowable-dnssec-parameters-01`: Allowable DNSSEC Parameters in EPP
*Presentation: [draft-jabley-regext-allowable-dnssec-parameters-01](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-regext-draft-jabley-regext-allowable-dnssec-parameters-00-01) by Joe Abley*

- **Problem Statement**: Registries currently use disparate, unpublished allow-lists for DNSSEC algorithms and digest types in EPP DS data, blocking operational testing and deployment of new algorithms (e.g., Algorithm 18 for post-quantum DNSSEC).
- **Proposal**: Provides algorithmic selection guidance by referencing machine-readable IANA registries updated under RFC 8624.
- **Discussion**: Jim Gould supported the proposal while suggesting relaxation of the proposed 30-day update timer and heavy DNSSEC Practice Statement (DPS) maintenance requirements. Paweł Kowalski noted that registries may still require upfront operational testing before accepting new parameters.

